Make these source-supported comparison differences visibly distinct in objects, positions, connections, sequence, or boundaries: outer shoe surface is visibly dry while enclosed inner regions retain visible moisture marks; the dry surface is outside the shoe boundary while the wetter toe, insole-below, and lining–midsole regions are contained inside it.

